+ * @cs_base: its cs_base, likewise
+ * @flags: its flags, likewise
+ *
+ * The TB-ending sequence of an indirect branch: what tcg_gen_lookup_and_goto_ptr()
+ * does through helper_lookup_tb_ptr(), emitted inline (M9 track, patch 20). The
+ * jump-cache entry of @pc is compared with (@pc, @cs_base, @flags) and the CPU's
+ * tcg_cflags, and the code jumps to the found TB, or to the epilogue when the
+ * entry does not match, a breakpoint exists or gdb single-step is on — the main
+ * loop's lookup is then the slow path (it fills the cache), exactly as when the
+ * helper finds no TB. The target computes the three inputs exactly as its
+ * cpu_get_tb_cpu_state() does, as TCG ops, so the result of the probe is the
+ * result the helper would have had. Falls back to the helper when the property
+ * inline-lookup is off, the TB may not use goto_ptr, exec logging or nochain is
+ * on (the helper logs every TB), or the host is not 64-bit.
+ */
+void translator_lookup_and_goto_ptr(TCGv_i64 pc, TCGv_i64 cs_base,
+                                    TCGv_i32 flags);
